-- Day notes of the three trip reports, rewritten as first-person travel memories.
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I started in the center of Beijing at the Forbidden City, the huge imperial palace with its courtyards and halls. From there I crossed Tiananmen Square and passed the Zhengyang Gate to the south. I finished at Jingshan Park, where the hill gives a wide view back over the palace roofs.' WHERE id = 1;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day at the Summer Palace, the large imperial garden in the northwest of Beijing. It is built around a lake, with temples and pavilions along the shore and on the hills. I walked the grounds slowly, because there is far more to see than a single visit covers.' WHERE id = 2;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took a day trip out of Beijing to the Mutianyu section of the Great Wall. It lies northeast of the city and follows the ridges of the mountains. I walked along the wall and looked out over the hills on both sides.' WHERE id = 3;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the morning train from Beijing to Pingyao. Pingyao is a walled city with well-preserved traditional buildings. I used the afternoon to walk the old streets inside the walls.' WHERE id = 4;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the afternoon train from Pingyao to Xi''an. Xi''an is an old imperial capital and still has its walled center. I used the evening to arrive and settle in.' WHERE id = 5;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I went out to the Terracotta Army, the life-size clay warriors that guard the tomb of Qin Shi Huang, China''s first emperor. The tomb complex of the emperor is part of the same visit. In the evening I saw The Song of Everlasting Regret, an outdoor historical performance near Huaqing Palace.' WHERE id = 6;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in the historic center of Xi''an. I saw the Bell and Drum Tower, visited the Tibetan Buddhist temple Guang Ren Si and walked on the ancient city walls. In the evening I went to Datang Everbright City, lit up in Tang-dynasty style, and ate at the Yongxingfang food street.' WHERE id = 7;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the Giant Wild Goose Pagoda and the plaza around it. It is one of the main Buddhist landmarks of Xi''an. In the evening I took the train to Chengdu.' WHERE id = 8;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I explored central Chengdu on foot. I walked across Jiuyan Bridge on the Jinjiang River, visited Daci Temple and shopped around Chunxi Road Taikoo Li. I ended the day on the Chengdu 339 observation deck, which gives a view over the skyline.' WHERE id = 9;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I started at the Chengdu Research Base of Giant Panda Breeding, a major panda conservation and viewing center. Later I walked through the old and new alleys of Kuanzhai Alley and sat in the teahouse atmosphere of People''s Park. I also stopped at SKP, an upscale mall in the center.' WHERE id = 10;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the temples and gardens of Chengdu. The Wenshu Monastery and the Taoist Qingyang Palace are both old and active places. I also saw the Du Fu Thatched Cottage, a memorial park for the Tang poet, and the Huanhuaxi Park next to it, and finished at Tianfu Square.' WHERE id = 11;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the morning train from Chengdu to the Huanglong area. Huanglong sits high in the mountains and is known for its colorful travertine pools. The altitude and the scenery made it a very different day from the city.' WHERE id = 12;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the whole day in Jiuzhaigou, a national park in northern Sichuan. The valley is known for its lakes and waterfalls. I walked between viewpoints and moved through the park at my own pace.' WHERE id = 13;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the morning train from Jiuzhaigou back to Chengdu. It was a travel day with no sightseeing planned. I spent the rest of the day in the city.' WHERE id = 14;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the morning train from Chengdu to Leshan to see the Leshan Grand Buddha. The statue is carved into the cliff and is enormous. In the afternoon I took the train to Chongqing and saw Chaotianmen Square by the river.' WHERE id = 15;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I explored the old parts of Chongqing on foot. I walked the stepped streets of Shibati and the revived Baixiang Street, and saw the Liziba monorail that runs through a building. I also visited Jiefangbei, Bayi Square, the creative district Xiahaoli and the old town of Ciqikou, known for narrow streets and local food.' WHERE id = 16;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I walked the viewpoints of Chongqing. Eling Park has city views and walking paths. I also visited Testbed 2, a creative park in a former industrial complex, and ended the day at HongyaDong, the multi-level complex of shops and lights.' WHERE id = 17;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the morning train from Chongqing to Wulong for a day among karst formations. I saw the Three Natural Bridges and walked the Longshui Gorge Seam, a deep gorge with walkways and elevators. In the afternoon I took the train back to Chongqing.' WHERE id = 18;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the afternoon train from Chongqing to Zhangjiajie. In the evening I saw TianMen Fox Fairy, a large outdoor musical staged around Tianmen Mountain. It was a good way to start my time in the area.' WHERE id = 19;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day on Tianmen Mountain, which has steep cliffs and is reached by cable car. I walked the cliff walkways and went to Heaven''s Gate. The views over the valley were wide and clear.' WHERE id = 20;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I went into Zhangjiajie National Forest Park, known for its tall pillar-like peaks. I rode the Bailong Elevator, a glass elevator on the cliff, and visited Yuanjiajie and Tianzi Shan for peak views. I also walked through the Shili Gallery, a valley corridor with shuttle and walking paths.' WHERE id = 21;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the Zhangjiajie Glass Bridge, which crosses the Grand Canyon. Then I went to Baofeng Lake, where boats move between karst hills. It was a day of views over water and rock.' WHERE id = 22;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I walked the park trails of Zhangjiajie. I went up to Huangshizhai, a high plateau with classic panoramas, and then followed the Golden Whip Stream trail. In the afternoon I took the train to Changsha.' WHERE id = 23;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited Changsha''s riverside and hills. I walked on Juzizhou Island in the Xiang River and went up Yuelu Mountain, which overlooks the river. I also saw Yuelu Academy, a historic academy with a long tradition of teaching.' WHERE id = 24;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I walked through central Changsha. I saw the Du Fu Jiangge pavilion by the river and ate around Wen Heyou, a multi-level food complex. I also walked Taiping Old Street and the busy squares Wuyi and Bayi, then took the evening train to Nanchang.' WHERE id = 25;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I explored the historic center of Nanchang around the Gan River. I visited Wanshou Palace, an old temple and old-town area. I also saw Tengwang Pavilion, the famous riverside landmark, and the Qiushui Square next to it.' WHERE id = 26;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I arrived in Xi''an and checked in. I used the day to settle in and rest. Xi''an is an old capital with a walled center, and I started here for the trip west.' WHERE id = 48;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I made a day trip from Xi''an to Huashan, one of the famous mountains of China. I climbed in the mountains and looked at the steep granite peaks. Then I returned to Xi''an in the evening.' WHERE id = 49;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the Shaanxi Museum, the major museum of the history of Shaanxi province, in Xi''an. In the afternoon I took the train to Xining. Xining is the gateway to Qinghai.' WHERE id = 50;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I drove a scenic route through the highlights of Qinghai. I stopped at Riyue Shan, the Sun and Moon Mountain area, and at Qinghai Lake, a large lake at high altitude. I ended at Chaka Salt Lake, where the salt flats reflect the sky like a mirror.' WHERE id = 51;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited Charhan Salt Lake, a salt lake in the high desert of Qinghai. I also stopped at Lonely Star, a spot on the road through the area. The landscape was wide, dry and almost empty.' WHERE id = 52;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I drove from Qinghai towards Dunhuang across the desert. On the way I saw the yardang landforms, which the wind has carved out of the rock. I also saw Heidu Mountain, a black mountain landscape near Dunhuang.' WHERE id = 53;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in Dunhuang. I visited the Mogao Caves, the famous Buddhist cave temples cut into the cliff. I climbed the Mingsha dunes, which sing when sand moves, and ended the evening at the Shazhou night market.' WHERE id = 54;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I followed the Silk Road around Dunhuang. I visited the Silk Road Heritage City and the old frontier passes Yangguan and Yumenguan. I ended in the Dunhuang Yadan geological park, with its eroded rock formations.' WHERE id = 55;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I traveled towards Jiayuguan with several stops on the way. I saw Son of Earth, a large art installation in the desert, and the ancient Yulin Caves. I ended at Jiayuguan Fortress, which stands at the western end of the Great Wall.' WHERE id = 56;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the Overhanging Great Wall, a section of the wall built on steep terrain. Then I went to Zhangye Danxia, where the hills are striped in red, orange and yellow. The colors are strongest in the light.' WHERE id = 57;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited Mati Temple, a temple and grotto site in the region. Then I crossed the Qilian Great Steppe, with wide grasslands and mountains in view. I ended the day in Xining.' WHERE id = 58;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in Xining. I visited the Dongguan Great Mosque, the main mosque of the city. I also went to Kumbum Monastery, an important Tibetan Buddhist monastery near Xining, and to the Xining wildlife park.' WHERE id = 59;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I traveled to Lanzhou and explored the city. I crossed the Zhongshan Bridge over the Yellow River and went up Baitashan Park for views of the city. I also saw the Yellow River Tower and walked the Lanzhou old street, a place for walking and eating.' WHERE id = 60;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I traveled from Lanzhou back to Xi''an. The journey took most of the day. It was a travel day with no sightseeing.' WHERE id = 61;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'This was the last day of the trip. I left Xi''an on an evening flight. The trip began and ended in the same city.' WHERE id = 62;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I started in Central Hong Kong, riding the trams along Des Voeux Road Central by day. The road is the main commercial corridor of the island. In the evening I went to Quarry Bay to see the Monster Building, a dense residential complex with a striking look.' WHERE id = 63;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took the Ngong Ping 360 cable car on Lantau Island to the Tian Tan Buddha, a large seated Buddha statue. In the evening I went up Victoria Peak, the famous viewpoint over the city. I stayed for the evening skyline.' WHERE id = 64;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the morning on Cheung Chau, an island with a harbor skyline and a waterfront. In the evening I was in Guangzhou at the Haixinsha Asian Games Park, a riverside park on the Pearl River. I also saw the Canton Tower, the tall observation tower of the city.' WHERE id = 65;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited Shamian Dao, a historic island district in Guangzhou with colonial-era buildings. I also went to the Nanyue King Museum, which covers the history of the Nanyue Kingdom. I spent the night at the Royal Hot Springs, a hot spring resort in Zhuhai.' WHERE id = 66;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in Macao, which mixes old and new. In the morning I visited the Monte Fortress, the Ruins of St. Paul''s and Senado Square, and the Garden of the Golden Chambers. Later I saw the Grand Lisboa, the Lotus Garden and the Eiffel Tower replica at The Parisian.' WHERE id = 67;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I made a short stop in Humen, between Macao and Shenzhen. The town sits on the Pearl River estuary. It was a brief break in the journey through the Pearl River Delta.' WHERE id = 68;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I explored Shenzhen. I walked in Lianhuashan Park, on the hill with the city views and the statue of Deng Xiaoping. I also went to Talent Park on Shenzhen Bay with a view of the Ping An Finance Center, then to Splendid China Folk Village and Huaqiang Road, the electronics street.' WHERE id = 69;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took a long train ride from Shenzhen towards Kunming. The route goes west across southern China. It was a full day of travel on the train.' WHERE id = 70;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in the Shilin Stone Forest, a karst landscape outside Kunming. It has pillars and formations of gray limestone that look like a forest. I walked the paths between the rocks.' WHERE id = 71;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I explored Kunming. I walked in Green Lake Park and in Kunming Old Street, a historic pedestrian and food area. I also went up the Xishan hills with the Longmen Grottoes above Dianchi Lake, and visited the Dounan Flower Market.' WHERE id = 72;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I arrived in Dali and settled into the Old Town. Dali is a town between the mountains and Erhai Lake. I walked the old streets in the evening, where lanterns hang over the lanes.' WHERE id = 73;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the Three Pagodas of Chongsheng Temple, the famous temple complex of Dali. From the temple I had views over Erhai Lake. I spent the rest of the day around the lake.' WHERE id = 74;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I traveled around Erhai Lake. I visited Xizhou Old Town with its traditional Bai architecture, Shuanglang Ancient Town on the shore and Jinshuo Island. I also stopped at the Luoquan Peninsula, Lixiangbang and Caicun Wharf.' WHERE id = 75;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in Lijiang Old Town, a historic town listed by UNESCO. I walked along the canals and the wooden lanes. There are flowers everywhere and the old streets are easy to get lost in.' WHERE id = 76;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I went to Jade Dragon Snow Mountain, a large mountain with glaciers near Lijiang. I also visited Blue Moon Valley, a valley with striking turquoise water. The snow peaks stood over the valley all day.' WHERE id = 77;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited the prayer flags of Lijiang and Dragon Girl Lake, an alpine lake near Jade Dragon Snow Mountain. After that I went to two ancient towns near Lijiang. Shuhe is an old Naxi town, and Baisha is quiet and historic.' WHERE id = 78;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I took a day trip to Lugu Lake, a mountain lake in the Yunnan highlands. I spent the day around its alpine shores. The water was clear and the mountains were close.' WHERE id = 79;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I walked part of Tiger Leaping Gorge, a dramatic canyon and hiking area with Haba Snow Mountain above it. Then I visited Baishuitai, the white travertine terraces. I ended the day in Dukezong Ancient City, a Tibetan-style old town in Shangri-La.' WHERE id = 80;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I visited Songzanlin, a large Tibetan Buddhist monastery near Shangri-La, and the Tower of Harmony. Then I went to Napa Lake and the Napa Grassland, a seasonal wetland and highland meadow. It was a day of temples and open land.' WHERE id = 81;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I spent the day in Potatso National Park, a protected area of lakes, forest and meadows. I walked the snowy boardwalks around Shuduhu Lake, an alpine lake inside the park. It was cold and the snow lay on the paths.' WHERE id = 82;
UPDATE days SET notes = 'I returned to Kunming. I visited Kunming Zoo, a popular park in the center of the city. It was a quiet last day on the road.' WHERE id = 83;
